ts", "children": [], "description": "Story points identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within estimation. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After analogous/parametric, story points supplies what is needed to address uncertainty ranges."}, {"id": "51cb559b-8f5e-49b5-8fd1-3ebfa7248212", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Uncertainty ranges", "children": [], "description": "Uncertainty ranges makes the validity limits of estimation explicit, showing when an otherwise correct method or system can become unreliable. After story points, uncertainty ranges supplies what is needed to address contingency."}, {"id": "b32bd40e-aa79-4cf4-8e71-c984787941bd", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Contingency", "children": [], "description": "Contingency identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within estimation. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. As the final topic in this module, contingency carries the completed idea into scheduling and dependencies."}]}, {"id": "76fc1c05-1e6c-44f6-9ee3-eeac1cac2043", "type": "topic", "title": "Scheduling and dependencies", "description": "This module builds directly on estimation and develops scheduling and dependencies. It belongs here because its methods and distinctions are prerequisites for budget and procurement.", "children": [{"id": "d55e29ba-42a9-4559-868a-69bc03122e28", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Network diagrams", "children": [], "description": "Network diagrams gives scheduling and dependencies a reusable representation for organizing assumptions, variables, and relationships before analysis begins. It appears before critical path because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "94a50833-dd17-46f8-88c4-3c25c3a1d7dd", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Critical path", "children": [], "description": "Critical path identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within schedul